---
import BaseLayout from '@/components/BaseLayout.astro';
import { media } from '@/data/media';
---

<BaseLayout>
    <section class="page-intro shell">
      <span class="record-number">TB / PROFILE / 2026</span>
      <div class="page-intro-grid page-intro-grid--profile">
        <h1>SYSTEMS<br />ACROSS<br />DOMAINS.</h1>

        <div class="about-intro-profile">
          <img
            src={media.portrait.src}
            alt={media.portrait.alt}
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <div class="about-identity">
            <p>
              Tyson Barnes is a systems engineer and systems architect working across physical,
              computational, operational and observational systems.
            </p>
            <span class="meta">SOUTH AFRICA / UNITED KINGDOM</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell about-ledger">
        <article class="about-prose">
          <span class="eyebrow">METHOD / CONTINUITY</span>
          <p class="about-lead">
            My work began in industrial instrumentation and process control, where failure is
            physical and systems have to work. That engineering discipline now extends across
            software engineering, Linux infrastructure, networks, operational systems,
            AI-assisted engineering and technical products.
          </p>
          <p>
            The disciplines differ, but the method remains consistent: understand the process,
            identify the interfaces, make state visible, remove unnecessary complexity, and leave
            something that can be operated.
          </p>
          <p>
            Nearly three years of practical live blood analysis and microscopy work have added a
            biological and observational dimension to the practice. On this site that work is
            presented as observation and practitioner experience, not as a substitute for
            laboratory diagnosis or medical care.
          </p>
        </article>

        <aside class="about-facts">
          <section>
            <span class="eyebrow">ENGINEERING FOUNDATION</span>
            <p>Red Seal Instrumentation Mechanician · Industrial Instrumentation &amp; Process Control</p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="eyebrow">CURRENT PRACTICE</span>
            <p>Systems Architecture · Software Engineering · Infrastructure · Applied AI</p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="eyebrow">OPERATING CONTEXT</span>
            <p>Industrial · Commercial · Health Practice · Independent Technical Products</p>
          </section>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--paper">
      <div class="shell">
        <header class="section-header">
          <div><span class="eyebrow">CAPABILITY / PRACTICE</span><h2>FIVE<br />FIELDS</h2></div>
          <p>
            Capability is presented through systems, records and shipped work rather than
            percentage bars or technology-logo inventories.
          </p>
        </header>

        <div class="capability-ledger">
          <section>
            <span>01</span><h3>PHYSICAL SYSTEMS</h3>
            <p>Instrumentation, process control, PLC systems, filtration, tribology, calibration, failure analysis and technical design.</p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span>02</span><h3>SOFTWARE &amp; INFRASTRUCTURE</h3>
            <p>Software engineering, Linux, systems administration, networking, web systems, hosting, mobile systems and automation.</p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span>03</span><h3>AI &amp; DATA SYSTEMS</h3>
            <p>Applied AI engineering, agentic development, human–AI workflows, data systems, verification and automation.</p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span>04</span><h3>OPERATIONAL SYSTEMS</h3>
            <p>ERP, POS, inventory, revenue control, SOP design, hospitality systems and business process architecture.</p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span>05</span><h3>OBSERVATIONAL PRACTICE</h3>
            <p>Live blood analysis, microscopy, photography, field observation and technical documentation.</p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section about-closing">
      <div class="shell about-closing-grid">
        <header>
          <span class="eyebrow">PRACTICE / EVIDENCE</span>
          <h2>THE WORK<br />IS THE RECORD.</h2>
        </header>

        <div class="about-closing-copy">
          <p>
            The common thread is systems work under real constraints: understanding a process,
            exposing its state, reducing unnecessary complexity and leaving something operable.
          </p>

          <p>
            This site is the working record. Systems document things built. Notes preserve
            engineering arguments, observations and experiments. Photography records what is
            better shown than explained.
          </p>

          <nav class="about-routes" aria-label="Explore the work">
            <a href="/systems/">
              <span class="meta">01 / BUILT</span>
              <strong>SYSTEMS</strong>
              <span>Engineered systems, software and infrastructure →</span>
            </a>

            <a href="/notes/">
              <span class="meta">02 / WRITTEN</span>
              <strong>NOTES</strong>
              <span>Arguments, lessons, observations and experiments →</span>
            </a>

            <a href="/photography/">
              <span class="meta">03 / OBSERVED</span>
              <strong>PHOTOGRAPHY</strong>
              <span>Photographic records and field observation →</span>
            </a>
          </nav>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>
